Suppress the XACT init error log on a headless game without audio content

A game installed without Content/XACT (a headless server) throws FileNotFoundException in
Game1.InitializeSounds, catches it, and falls back to its dummy audio engine; the catch logs
the exception as an error, which SMAPI prints as [ERROR game]. The fallback is the expected
state on such an install, so drop that one log line the same way SGameLogger drops the
Steam-not-loaded one. Any other XACT failure (content present) still logs.

diff --git a/src/SMAPI/Framework/SGameLogger.cs b/src/SMAPI/Framework/SGameLogger.cs
index 1949078..d181450 100644
--- a/src/SMAPI/Framework/SGameLogger.cs
+++ b/src/SMAPI/Framework/SGameLogger.cs
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 using System;
+using System.IO;
 using StardewModdingAPI.Internal;
 using StardewValley.Logging;
 
@@ -64,6 +65,11 @@ internal class SGameLogger : IGameLogger
             );
         }
 
+        // game without audio content (a headless install strips Content/XACT): the game already fell
+        // back to its dummy audio engine, so the missing wave bank is expected there
+        else if (error == "Game.Initialize() caught exception initializing XACT." && exception is FileNotFoundException)
+            return;
+
         // any other error
         else
         {
